A||||4||noyb||Another brake question.||||1||
Z||000000||noyb||03-18-2001||11:42 AM||||Just did a complete brake job on my 87GT.  All new rotors and pads, plus one new caliper.  Bled all four brakes repeatedly.  However, I still have what I consider to be excess brake pedal travel and "mushy" brakes.  Just seems to take more pressure than it should to stop.  I'm not sure I could lock the wheels up if I wanted to.  Open for thoughts and opinions on this issue.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||KRMFiero||03-18-2001||12:59 PM||||Stainless Steel Brake lines from the Fiero store should fix it.<P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red)<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>     <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||voyagerspe||03-18-2001||01:08 PM||||I agree, "earl's" ss brake lines from the fiero store took the mush out of my brakes.  but even New rubber lines should help if your on a budget.<p>[This message has been edited by voyagerspe (edited 03-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||03-18-2001||01:22 PM||||read the notes in my cave. If you got air in the MC it can be hard to get out. It is also posible the MC may be starting to fail.<P>If the lines are cruddy then replacing them is always a good idea. They should be replaced if they even look bad... cacks down to cording are a really bad thing. That should always mean imediate replacement.<P>New OE lines will have about the same result as the new SS lines. I've used SS and OE replacements I doubt anyone could actually feel a diferance. SS lines look nice but I have my doubts about how well they last. I've used a good amount of SS line for brakes and fuel. If they aren't installed carfully they can wear thru allot faster than many people think. One thing I consider a must is putting a section of rubber line on the section that passes thru the support bracket. I usually use a piece of split fuel line. Anything to protect the line from rubbing or having a sharp edge to bend against. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||noyb||03-18-2001||04:52 PM||||Thanks for all of your replies!  I just purchased this vehicle from someone who totally ignored maintenance.  I've just started the long process of fixing everything.  New brake lines it is.  I'll be posting more questions in the future.||||reg||7
